# Resume versioning

- The master inventory is `resumes/base/JZ_resume.tex`. It is not Polar's
  required attach.
- One active master on disk. `JZ_resume` at `resumes/base/JZ_resume.tex`
  and `resumes/base/JZ_resume.pdf`.
- `role_cluster` / `resume_cluster` are historical job taxonomy only (`cloud_swe` | `data_ml` | `health_ai`). They are not the production router.
- `resume_family` is the discovery-time route (`swe` | `ml_ai` | `ai_infra` | `health_ai` | `REVIEW`). Policy: `knowledge/resume_routing.yaml`. Docs: `docs/resume/ROUTING.md`.
- Prefer the Simplify resume already attached. Do not upload the two-page
  master. Empty widget → REVIEW_READY / `missing_production_resume`.
- After BUILD exists, production disk attach is a frozen family one-pager
  or a human-accepted VIP file.
- Register a `data/resume_versions.csv` row only after a human accepts the
  file. The engine does not append that row.
- Historical `resume_version` strings on applied rows stay. Inactive
  registry rows stay. Do not regenerate the cluster tree.
- Record exact `resume_version` after every apply.
- Every new version needs a hypothesis in `data/resume_versions.csv`.
